WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
AI Incident Investigator — local MVP
A real model response on synthetic demo telemetry.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Choose the service and environment.
Menus float above the form and support keyboard navigation.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:31.000
The test creates a fresh Java order that returns simulated HTTP 504.
The order ID links the investigation to its exact log records.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Investigate sends one browser request to the Python backend.
Logs, Prometheus summaries and current Actuator snapshots reach the real model.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:57.000
The report retains evidence from all three sources.
The animation shows activity and returned counts, not live per-source progress.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Open a log to inspect its source reference and timestamp.
The timeout is explicitly marked as simulated.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:25.000
AI interpretation still requires engineering review.
Successful scrapes do not prove continuous business health.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Known model limitation: heap was called stable without a baseline.
Check every claim against the linked observations before acting.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Collection gaps remain visible; traces are not connected.
Current Actuator snapshots cannot reconstruct historical health.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Export JSON preserves the original request and unedited report.
Read-only assistance: no automatic repair, deployment or on-call paging.

